          "path": "_m/x/n/7/7/mode-gakuen-cocoon-tower-wp/mode-gakuen-cocoon-tow-2.jpg",
          "filename": "Mode Gakuen Cocoon Tower in the evening with blue sky Tokyo Japan.jpg",
          "caption": "Mode Gakuen Cocoon Tower in the evening with blue sky. This skyscraper is a 204 metres (669 feet), 50-story educational facility located in the Nishi-Shinjuku district in Shinjuku, Tokyo, Japan. The building is home to three educational institutions: Tokyo Mode Gakuen (fashion vocational school), HAL Tokyo (special technology and design college), and Shuto Ikō (medical college). Completed in October 2008, the tower is the second-tallest educational building in the world and is the 17th-tallest building in Tokyo in 2020. It was awarded the 2008 Skyscraper of the Year by Emporis.",
          "alt": "Mode Gakuen Cocoon Tower in the evening with blue sky. This skyscraper is a 204 metres (669 feet), 50-story educational facility located in the Nishi-Shinjuku district in Shinjuku, Tokyo, Japan. The building is home to three educational institutions: Tokyo Mode Gakuen (fashion vocational school), HAL Tokyo (special technology and design college), and Shuto Ikō (medical college). Completed in October 2008, the tower is the second-tallest educational building in the world and is the 17th-tallest building in Tokyo in 2020. It was awarded the 2008 Skyscraper of the Year by Emporis.",
